# Unsafe Pattern Refactoring Guide

## Linked List Iteration

c2rust generates awkward list traversal. When refactoring:

```rust
// Before (c2rust style):
let mut item = database_list.head.next;
while item != &raw mut database_list.head {
    let db = (item as *mut c_char).offset(-(0 as c_ulong as isize)) as *mut PgDatabase;
    // ... use db ...
    item = (*item).next;
}

// After (when list abstraction exists):
for db in database_list.iter() {
    // ... use db ...
}
```

## Null Pointer Checks

```rust
// Before:
if !ptr.is_null() {
    let val = (*ptr).field;
}

// After (with Option<&T>):
if let Some(obj) = ptr.as_ref() {
    let val = obj.field;
}

// Or with early return:
let obj = ptr.as_ref()?;
let val = obj.field;
```

## Function Pointers

```rust
// Before:
(*lookup).func.expect("non-null function pointer")(admin, arg)

// After (when refactoring callback system):
(lookup.func)(admin, arg)
// Or use closures/traits when redesigning
```

## Buffer Operations

```rust
// Before:
let mut buf: [c_char; 1024] = [0; 1024];
vsnprintf(&raw mut buf as *mut c_char, size_of::<[c_char; 1024]>() as size_t, fmt, ap);

// After (eventual goal):
let msg = format!("{}", args);
// or use a proper buffer type
```

## Cast Chains

c2rust produces excessive casts. Simplify when types are known:

```rust
// Before:
len as c_ulong as usize

// After:
len as usize

// Before:
0 as c_int as c_uint

// After:
0u32
```

## Struct Field Access Through Pointers

```rust
// Before:
(*socket).state = STATE_ACTIVE;
(*(*socket).pool).db_name

// After (with references):
socket.state = State::Active;
socket.pool.db_name
```

## Mutable Static Access

```rust
// Before:
unsafe { cf_verbose = 1; }

// After (thread-local):
CF_VERBOSE.with(|v| *v.borrow_mut() = 1);

// For read access:
let verbose = CF_VERBOSE.with(|v| *v.borrow());
```

## Pointer-to-Reference Conversion

Only convert when you can prove the pointer is valid and properly aligned:

```rust
// Safe to convert when:
// 1. Pointer is known non-null (checked or from reference)
// 2. Lifetime is properly bounded
// 3. No aliasing violations

// Before:
unsafe fn process(ptr: *mut Foo) {
    if ptr.is_null() { return; }
    (*ptr).field = value;
}

// After:
fn process(foo: Option<&mut Foo>) {
    if let Some(f) = foo {
        f.field = value;
    }
}

// Or with non-optional:
fn process(foo: &mut Foo) {
    foo.field = value;
}
```

## String Handling

```rust
// Before (C string literal):
b"SELECT 1\0" as *const u8 as *const c_char

// Intermediate (still needs C compat):
c"SELECT 1".as_ptr()

// After (pure Rust):
"SELECT 1"
```

## Conditional Compilation Remnants

Remove platform-specific type modules when consolidating:

```rust
// Remove these c2rust-generated modules:
#[c2rust::header_src = "/...MacOSX.sdk/.../types.h"]
pub mod _types_h { ... }

// Replace with direct Rust types in the code that uses them
```
